{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QACkkPSrSBepgR2VCjvUUA","type":"tool_result","content":"    raise TypeError(\"Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\")\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\nAttributeError: module 'app' has no attribute 'to_dynamo'\nFAIL: test_second_publish_stores_float_free_similar (test_publish.PublishTest.test_second_publish_stores_float_free_similar)\nAssertionError: 500 != 201 : {'statusCode': 500, 'body': '{\"error\": \"Internal Server Error\"}'}\n M src/app.py\n M tests/test_publish.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aaa753eb-1f0e-456d-bc66-c2db22d18176","uuid":"3f23f4fd-7220-499c-8607-fbd35873c83e","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:14:21.541Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"    raise TypeError(\"Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\")\nTypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.\nAttributeError: module 'app' has no attribute 'to_dynamo'\nFAIL: test_second_publish_stores_float_free_similar (test_publish.PublishTest.test_second_publish_stores_float_free_similar)\nAssertionError: 500 != 201 : {'statusCode': 500, 'body': '{\"error\": \"Internal Server Error\"}'}\n M src/app.py\n M tests/test_publish.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01QACkkPSrSBepgR2VCjvUUA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSAtKV9qpjh5VmzjkUev","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The regression test reproduces the 500 on the old code. Writing ANSWER.md."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":25891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":347},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aaa753eb-1f0e-456d-bc66-c2db22d18176","uuid":"1755e47e-ec6a-4f02-9256-ca24b96148ad","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:14:26.579Z","request_id":"req_011CgSAtKF1kSgCd1HUu4xZT"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgSAtKV9qpjh5VmzjkUev","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019R9Y4s81nCYQxeTujbrB9U","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-m1CH8a/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story together with `similar: [{slug, score}]`, and\n`score` comes from `similarity()`, which returns a Python `float`\n(`round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`). boto3's DynamoDB serializer\ndoesn't accept `float` anywhere in an item. It raises\n`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` That\nerror isn't a `ValueError`, so `handler()` catches it as a generic exception\nand returns 500.\n\nThe first publish works only because the library is empty. `scan()` returns\nnothing, so `similar == []` and the item contains no floats (`published_at` is\nan `int`). The log confirms it: `similar=0 stored`. From the second publish on\nthere is at least one other story, so `similar` holds a float score and\n`put_item` fails every time (09:21:47 and 09:22:10 in `logs/error.log`).\n\nThe existing test missed this because it only publishes into an empty table.\n\n## Fix (`src/app.py`)\n\n- New `to_dynamo()` function. It walks the item recursively and converts every\n  `float` to `Decimal(str(value))`. Going through `str` keeps the short form\n  (`0.4667`) instead of the binary expansion. `NaN`/`inf` are rejected with a\n  `ValueError` (→ 400), because DynamoDB can't store them either.\n- `publish()` runs the item through `to_dynamo()` right before\n  `table.put_item()`. The conversion happens at the database boundary rather\n  than inside `similarity()`, so any float field added to the item later is\n  converted automatically. That's what keeps this class of error from coming\n  back.\n- Items read back from DynamoDB already contain `Decimal`. They're only passed\n  to `similarity()`, which uses `slug`, `tags` and `body`, not `score`, so the\n  read path is unaffected.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_float_free_similar` publishes 3 stories in a row\n  through `handler()`. It checks that every call returns 201 and that\n  `similar[].score` is stored as a `Decimal`. On the old code it fails with\n  `500 != 201`, the same `TypeError` as in production.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_nested_floats` checks the conversion of nested\n  floats, and that `bool`/`int` values are left unchanged.\n\n`python3 -m unittest discover tests`: all 3 tests pass.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":347,"cache_read_input_tokens":25891,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":347},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"aaa753eb-1f0e-456d-bc66-c2db22d18176","uuid":"3147c951-f5ec-4073-b1fc-2d232ed6fdb3","timestamp":"2026-10-27T05:14:34.183Z","request_id":"req_011CgSAtKF1kSgCd1HUu4xZT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019R9Y4s81nCYQxeTujbrB9U":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-m1CH8a/ANSWER.md","content":"# Why the second publish returns 500\n\n## Cause\n\n`publish()` stores each story together with `similar: [{slug, score}]`, and\n`score` comes from `similarity()`, which returns a Python `float`\n(`round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)`). boto3's DynamoDB serializer\ndoesn't accept `float` anywhere in an item. It raises\n`TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` That\nerror isn't a `ValueError`, so `handler()` catches it as a generic exception\nand returns 500.\n\nThe first publish works only because the library is empty. `scan()` returns\nnothing, so `similar == []` and the item contains no floats (`published_at` is\nan `int`). The log confirms it: `similar=0 stored`. From the second publish on\nthere is at least one other story, so `similar` holds a float score and\n`put_item` fails every time (09:21:47 and 09:22:10 in `logs/error.log`).\n\nThe existing test missed this because it only publishes into an empty table.\n\n## Fix (`src/app.py`)\n\n- New `to_dynamo()` function. It walks the item recursively and converts every\n  `float` to `Decimal(str(value))`. Going through `str` keeps the short form\n  (`0.4667`) instead of the binary expansion. `NaN`/`inf` are rejected with a\n  `ValueError` (→ 400), because DynamoDB can't store them either.\n- `publish()` runs the item through `to_dynamo()` right before\n  `table.put_item()`. The conversion happens at the database boundary rather\n  than inside `similarity()`, so any float field added to the item later is\n  converted automatically. That's what keeps this class of error from coming\n  back.\n- Items read back from DynamoDB already contain `Decimal`. They're only passed\n  to `similarity()`, which uses `slug`, `tags` and `body`, not `score`, so the\n  read path is unaffected.\n\n## Tests (`tests/test_publish.py`)\n\n- `test_second_publish_stores_float_free_similar` publishes 3 stories in a row\n  through `handler()`. It checks that every call returns 201 and that\n  `similar[].score` is stored as a `Decimal`. On the old code it fails with\n  `500 != 201`, the same `TypeError` as in production.\n- `test_to_dynamo_converts_nested_floats` checks the conversion of nested\n  floats, and that `bool`/`int` values are left unchanged.\n\n`python3 -m unittest discover tests`: all 3 tests pass.\n"}}}
